---
description: Git hooks and Makefile CI gate rules
alwaysApply: true
---

- pre-commit → `make pre-commit` → `pnpm lint-staged`; failure blocks commit
- pre-push → `make pre-push` → full check + integration tests; failure blocks push (non-zero exit)
- post-merge → `pnpm graphify:update` when Graphify CLI is installed (optional, non-blocking)
- commit-msg → `pnpm commitlint`; failure blocks commit
- `make ci` MUST equal `make pre-push` — keep in sync
- Never use `--no-verify` unless user explicitly requests it
- Add new quality checks to Makefile `check` target; they flow into `pre-push` and `ci`

## CI gate (no UI tooling)

`make check` includes: lint, format, typecheck, security-audit, vitest unit tests.

`make pre-push` adds integration tests (`pnpm test:integration`).

There is no Storybook, i18n check, Playwright E2E, or a11y gate in this API-only project.
